WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.650
It'd be the showdown of the century — but
could the Mighty Adam really take on the Man of Steel?

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:10.042
Dwayne Johnson faced an eight-year struggle
to bring Black Adam to the big screen.

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:12.799
Now, Johnson's patience and dedication has
paid off.

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:18.980
In its first four days at the box office,
Black Adam brought in $67 million domestically,

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:23.320
becoming the best opening-weekend performance
of any movie with Johnson in the lead role.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.970
Notably, the character Johnson portrays, Black
Adam, is one of the most powerful in DC Comics.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:32.810
Of course, the biggest buzz behind Black Adam
is Superman's brief cameo at the very end

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:33.820
of the movie.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.170
It's a match made in heaven — in the comic
books, both characters possess superhuman

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.980
strength, speed, hearing, healing, and stamina.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.550
But the movie's tease of a showdown between
Supes and Mighty Adam has got fans wondering:

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.334
who will ultimately win when these two juggernauts
come to blows in the DCEU?

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:52.824
"There's no one on this planet that can stop
me."

00:00:52.824 --> 00:00:56.989
One critical difference between Superman and
Black Adam in the comics is that Adam can

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:01.420
discharge lightning bolts as projectiles while
engaging his enemies in battle.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.275
It might not ever need to come to that, though,
because Black Adam has an immediate edge over Kal-El.

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:11.080
The Mighty Adam's most significant, unique
advantage over the Last Son of Krypton is

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.810
that he is immortal.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:17.580
Superman seems ageless, but Kal-El does grow
older, albeit at a prolonged rate due to the

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.070
sun's effect on his Kryptonian cells.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:24.040
It might take centuries, or even longer, but
Clark Kent will eventually succumb to death

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.540
from natural causes.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:30.060
If a brouhaha between these two super beings
ever escalated into a fight, theoretically,

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.229
Black Adam could just wait it out until Superman
keels over from old age.

00:01:34.383 --> 00:01:38.141
Since a millennia-long wait does not make
for very good storytelling, however, there

00:01:38.141 --> 00:01:40.890
must be a more immediate determination of
a winner.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.180
For his part, Superman can put up one heck
of a fight.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:50.400
His debut in Action Comics #1 back in 1938
saw Superman able to "leap 1/8th of a mile,"

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.759
with skin that could be broken by "nothing
less than a bursting shell."

00:01:53.759 --> 00:01:58.399
By contrast, the Superman of more recent days
has been seen lifting quintillions of tons

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:02.850
single-handed, flying so fast that time moves
backward, and punching holes in the fabric

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.280
of reality.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.330
Writers have gone back to the "Superman loses
his powers" well so many times that it's become

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:12.200
a full-blown trope, mostly because it's hard
to write a high-stakes story when your hero

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.290
can't be beaten.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:16.340
And that might just be where Black Adam comes
into play.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:20.970
While everybody knows that Superman is vulnerable
to kryptonite, he has another weakness that

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.572
people often forget about: magic.

00:02:23.796 --> 00:02:29.069
In Superman #14, the Man of Steel was put
under a trance by malevolent fish people.

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:34.489
In Superman Vol. 2 #49, a piece of magical
Kryptonite strips him of his powers.

00:02:34.489 --> 00:02:39.430
In Superman #171, he outright laments that
his invulnerability can't protect him from

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.069
a sorcerer's spell.

00:02:41.069 --> 00:02:42.720
This brings us to Black Adam.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.570
Adam has gone through his own growing pains
over the years, but one aspect of his personality

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:50.140
has remained solid: His powers are magical
in nature.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.575
"Did he just catch a rocket?"

00:02:51.575 --> 00:02:52.519
"He caught a rocket."

00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:56.510
They were given to him by the same wizard
who turned Billy Batson into the World's Mightiest

00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:00.790
Mortal, and they stem from the abilities of
ancient gods — sometimes Greek, sometimes

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:03.760
Egyptian, but always very, very powerful.

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:08.569
If Black Adam plans on defeating Superman,
he should travel to Smallville, Kansas, where

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:13.420
Kal-El's vessel crash-landed on Earth — and
where he may find Green K Kryptonite.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.519
Green K is among the most common and powerful
iterations of Kryptonite because it can weaken

00:03:17.519 --> 00:03:20.540
and kill the Man of Steel with prolonged exposure.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.519
If the Mighty Adam wants to take out Superman
once and for all, though, there's only one

00:03:24.519 --> 00:03:28.450
shade of Kryptonite he should bother searching
for: Gold Kryptonite.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.260
The most formidable weapon Black Adam, or
anyone else for that matter, could ever hope

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:37.260
to wield against Kal-El, Gold Kryptonite will
permanently strip Superman of all his powers.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:41.769
Black Adam will have to get up close and personal
to use it, but Gold K is another potential

00:03:41.769 --> 00:03:42.769
way to victory.

00:03:42.909 --> 00:03:47.769
With all the advantages Black Adam has over
the Man of Steel, the simple truth remains:

00:03:47.769 --> 00:03:49.069
Superman is stronger.

00:03:49.069 --> 00:03:52.540
If it comes down to physical combat, the Mighty
Adam will fall.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:56.799
Even inferior, alternate versions of Superman
have bested Black Adam in the comic books.

00:03:56.799 --> 00:03:57.799
In Shazam!

00:03:57.799 --> 00:04:03.189
Vol. 3 #14, the evil Superboy-Prime easily
defeats not only Black Adam but all the Marvels

00:04:03.189 --> 00:04:04.222
on his own.

00:04:04.222 --> 00:04:08.239
And that was the second time Superboy-Prime
bested the Mighty Adam — he also made quick

00:04:08.239 --> 00:04:11.379
work of him during the Infinite Crisis crossover
event.

00:04:11.379 --> 00:04:16.040
Ultraman, Kal-El's alternate, darker half
from Earth-3, ended his fisticuffs with Black

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:19.329
Adam by breaking his jaw in Forever Evil #3.

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:23.830
And don't think Superman will have any problem
dealing out punishment against his new foe.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:28.130
Kal-El has abandoned his morality on multiple
occasions to do what is necessary to save

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.180
the world and those he loves.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:35.040
An alternate-reality Kal-El slaughtered Wonder
Woman in 2004's Superman/Batman: Absolute

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:39.780
Power, and the Man of Steel wiped out the
Joker, Black Canary, Green Arrow, and even

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.520
Shazam in the far-reaching Injustice saga.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:47.660
Finally, in Man of Steel, the first official
installment of the DCEU's big-screen adventures,

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:51.360
Superman is forced to break General Zod's
neck to save a group of civilians.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.571
Bottom line: Superman is not above killing.

00:04:54.682 --> 00:04:58.930
Although Dwayne Johnson put in a lot of work
to get Henry Cavill back in the game, the

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:03.540
answer to this question is simple: Given the
right conditions, Black Adam would best Superman

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:04.424
in a fight.

00:05:04.424 --> 00:05:07.480
Funnily enough, however, Johnson doesn't necessarily
agree.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:09.550
In an interview with Jake's Takes, he said:

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:14.619
"We will create Black Adam for him to be the
most powerful and unstoppable force on this planet.

00:05:14.619 --> 00:05:18.979
The most powerful and unstoppable force in
the entire universe has been on the sidelines

00:05:18.979 --> 00:05:19.979
for too long."

00:05:19.979 --> 00:05:23.850
So what's going to happen when Superman and
Black Adam finally get their showdown?

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.349
Looks like we'll just have to wait to find
out.

